How many times have we seen questions sent to rec.games.hack asking how to
run in wizard mode (hundreds?).  I think the code to let you select wizard
mode should be fixed.  Currently, if you give the "-D" option, and are not
authorized to run in wizard mode, you drop into discover mode.  I think
when the game does this, it should tell you WHY NOT!

On some systems, anyone typing "nethack -uwizard -D" can run in wizard 
mode.  On other multiuser systems, only a certain userid can use wizard
mode.  If you type "nethack -D", and don't get wizard mode, you should 
get one of the following messages, depending on the reason:

  "Type 'nethack -u[insert wizard name] -D' to run in wizard mode"
  "Only userid [insert userid] can use wizard mode"

Presto!  One FAQ could disappear.

Could we see this in 3.1.1 (the first 3.1.0 bug-fix version)?


(I don't know about the LINUX version, but on my system I replaced the word
 wizard with my userid, and it worked)
